    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "overview",
        "title": "The haunted help desk",
        "body": "# The haunted help desk\n\nA fictional support workflow for Harbor Notes.\n\n**Question:** How do I export my workspace?\n\nThe [[Kiro agent design]] describes how the assistant retrieves evidence before it writes a reply.\n\n## One connected workspace\n\nExplore the diagram, read the linked design notes, then open the architecture deck.",
        "updatedAt": 1794528000000
      },
      {
        "id": "agent_design",
        "title": "Kiro agent design",
        "body": "# Kiro agent design\n\nOne customer question. A grounded, cited answer.\n\n## How the agent works\n\n1. **Retrieve** documentation and related passages.\n2. **Draft** an answer from the ranked sources.\n3. **Check** citations before sending the reply.\n\n## Connected knowledge\n\nRead the [[Retrieval design]] or follow the [[Support runbook]]. Both pages are linked to the canvas.\n\n> Fold the system for the big picture. Unfold a group when you need the details.\n\n## Answer contract\n\nEvery reply follows the shared [[Response contract]].",
        "updatedAt": 1794528000000
      },
      {
        "id": "retrieval",
        "title": "Retrieval design",
        "body": "# Retrieval design\n\nCombine exact product terms with semantic matches.\n\n## Two complementary sources\n\n| Source | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| GitHub docs | Approved product documentation |\n| Vector index | Related passages and wording |\n\nMerge the results, remove duplicates, then rank the evidence.\n\nSee [[Hybrid search]] for the branch details.\n\n{{diagram:Search}}",
        "updatedAt": 1794528000000
      },
      {
        "id": "search",
        "title": "Hybrid search",
        "body": "# Hybrid search\n\nRun keyword and vector retrieval for the same customer question.\n\n## Search paths\n\n- **GitHub docs** preserve exact feature names.\n- **Vector index** finds related wording.\n- **Merge evidence** combines both result sets.\n\nThe parent [[Retrieval design]] ranks the merged sources.\n\n{{diagram:Search}}",
        "updatedAt": 1794528000000
      },
      {
        "id": "runbook",
        "title": "Support runbook",
        "body": "# Support runbook\n\n## When evidence is missing\n\n1. Check that GitHub documentation is available.\n2. Verify that the vector index is current.\n3. Ask a support specialist to review uncertain answers.\n\nReturn to [[Kiro agent design]] for the normal flow.",
        "updatedAt": 1794528000000
      },
      {
        "id": "contract",
        "title": "Response contract",
        "body": "# Response contract\n\nEvery customer reply must include:\n\n- A direct answer to the question.\n- Links to the supporting documentation.\n- A clear next step if human review is required.\n\nThe [[Kiro agent design]] and reply node share this page.",
        "updatedAt": 1794528000000
      }
    ],
    "decks": [
      {
        "id": "architecture",
        "title": "Inside the haunted help desk",
        "body": "---\ntitle: Inside the haunted help desk\nbackgroundColor: '#211a2b'\ncolor: '#f7e6cf'\nfont: sans\nheadingFont: sans\ntransition: fade\n---\n\n# Inside the haunted help desk\n\nOne question. One connected workflow.\n\n**Kiro agent · Architecture walkthrough**\n\n---\n\n# Retrieve. Draft. Verify.\n\n- **Retrieve** evidence from GitHub docs and a vector index.\n- **Draft** an answer grounded in ranked sources.\n- **Verify** citations before sending the reply.\n\nThe diagram, wiki pages, and deck share one workspace.\n\n---\n\n# One diagram, three levels\n\n| Level | What you see |\n| --- | --- |\n| Overview | The complete support workflow |\n| Retrieval | Rewrite, search, and ranking |\n| Search | GitHub docs and vector matches |\n\nKeep the diagram and its explanation in the same workspace.\n\n---\n\n# Share the flow\n\nExport an animated GIF for a README, design review, or team update.\n\n**Keep the context. Share the motion.**",
        "updatedAt": 1794528000000
      }
    ]
  }
